1
00:00:16,599 --> 00:00:19,492
Everything you'll see runs in this browser tab:

2
00:00:19,492 --> 00:00:21,462
a real Ethereum virtual machine,

3
00:00:21,462 --> 00:00:24,109
running exactly what the Fe compiler built.

4
00:00:24,372 --> 00:00:25,544
Let's draw a seven.

5
00:00:25,544 --> 00:00:27,887
The network runs the moment we let go:

6
00:00:27,887 --> 00:00:31,647
thirty-two hidden neurons, then ten outputs, all in integers.

7
00:00:31,906 --> 00:00:33,302
The network says seven.

8
00:00:33,302 --> 00:00:35,425
Right, and computed fully on-chain.

9
00:00:35,425 --> 00:00:36,941
That's the expensive way.

10
00:00:37,207 --> 00:00:39,487
Now let's lie, and claim it's a one.

11
00:00:39,487 --> 00:00:40,311
Not clumsily:

12
00:00:40,311 --> 00:00:42,211
we forge a few hidden neurons,

13
00:00:42,211 --> 00:00:44,997
then compute everything after them honestly.

14
00:00:44,997 --> 00:00:47,341
So the final answer looks consistent.

15
00:00:47,918 --> 00:00:51,118
We post the lie, with one ether of play money as the bond.

16
00:00:51,845 --> 00:00:55,160
A watcher re-runs the network off-chain, in WebAssembly,

17
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:57,883
and finds the first neuron that doesn't match.

18
00:00:58,148 --> 00:01:01,613
Challenge only the final answer, and the contract refuses.

19
00:01:01,613 --> 00:01:03,226
The lie is hidden upstream.

20
00:01:03,484 --> 00:01:05,278
So challenge the neuron itself.

21
00:01:05,278 --> 00:01:07,534
The contract checks the claim's hashes,

22
00:01:07,534 --> 00:01:10,484
proves the weights against the model's Merkle root,

23
00:01:10,484 --> 00:01:12,103
and re-runs that one neuron.

24
00:01:14,143 --> 00:01:14,595
Slashed.

25
00:01:14,595 --> 00:01:17,642
Half the bond goes to the watcher, and half is burned.

26
00:01:17,642 --> 00:01:21,141
It cost under a tenth of the gas of running the whole network.

27
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:23,435
Now an honest claim, for contrast.

28
00:01:23,435 --> 00:01:26,188
We post the truth, and try to break it anyway.

29
00:01:26,188 --> 00:01:29,480
The contract refuses the challenge, with its own error.

30
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:32,771
An hour later on the chain's clock, the claim is final.

31
00:01:35,535 --> 00:01:35,946
Why Fe?

32
00:01:35,946 --> 00:01:38,757
Shapes and fixed-point scales live in the types.

33
00:01:38,757 --> 00:01:42,213
Wire up a layer of the wrong shape, and it doesn't compile.

34
00:01:43,736 --> 00:01:47,591
Effects are in the signatures, so only withdraw can send ether.

35
00:01:47,591 --> 00:01:49,427
And the safety is almost free:

36
00:01:49,427 --> 00:01:51,630
about two percent of a neuron's gas.
